Metabolite-enzyme specificity, Cases = 11 (47.8%). Metabolite-enzyme specificity, Description = Qwen3-32B selects the positionally overlapping gene despite having no enzymatic role in the metabolite's production, degradation, or transport. BioBLIP selects the correct metabolic enzyme or transporter.. Multi-gene locus disambiguation, Cases = 6 (26.1%). Multi-gene locus disambiguation, Description = At loci with multiple neighboring genes, Qwen3-32B anchors on the overlapping gene and cannot override this choice even when it mentions the biologically relevant gene elsewhere in its trace.. Canonical GWAS locus recognition, Cases = 6 (26.1%). Canonical GWAS locus recognition, Description = At well-characterized loci with long-range regulatory effects (8q24, 9p21.3), Qwen3-32B selects a proximal neighbor or wrong paralog. BioBLIP's multimodal tokens appear to encode locus-level functional annota- tion that resolves these cases.

