Results and Observations. Results for all reasoning traces and non-closest gene traces are shown in Table 2. Notably, Bio-BLIP appears to leverage its multimodal architecture to achieve wins over Qwen3-32B in both overall accuracy (6.8% improvement). It also shows improvement on the more challenging set of non-closest gene traces (11.4% improvement). Bio-BLIP only lags behind the frontier model Claude in a total of nine non-closest gene traces. We used Claude Opus 4.6 to characterize the 23 non-closest gene traces where Bio-BLIP wins over Qwen3-32B, and illustrative traces relating to each pattern are shown in 6.

